{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>Behold, truth</b> — the meaning is: even though I have sinned, the faith of my heart in Your divinity has not gone astray, and this is what You desire and want from a person." "<b>In the hidden parts</b> — the concealed places, which are the seat of the heart. And our ancestors of blessed memory said: these are the kidneys, which are covered in fat, as in: 'Who puts wisdom in the hidden parts' (Job 38:36)." "<b>And in the hidden part</b> — teach me and make me know the thing hidden from me. And in my opinion: the meaning is doubled, and the tav of תודיעני — 'make me know' — returns to אמת, for its root is אמנה, and the tav is feminine, as in אמת מארץ תצמח (Psalms 85:12), in the manner of בת — and behold בתו is בנתו, and likewise אמתו, and in the plural one says אמנות, not אמתים, just as one does not say בת בתים but rather בנות."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 51, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:31:35.453581586Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}